<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <script type="application/ld+json">
      {
        "@context": "https://schema.org",
        "@type": "SoftwareApplication",
        "name": "nossl.sh",
        "applicationCategory": "DeveloperApplication",
        "operatingSystem": "Windows, macOS, Linux",
        "offers": { "@type": "Offer", "price": "0", "priceCurrency": "USD" },
        "url": "https://nossl.sh/",
        "publisher": {
          "@type": "Organization",
          "name": "nossl.sh",
          "url": "https://nossl.sh/"
        }
      }
    </script>
    <script type="application/ld+json">
      {
        "@context": "https://schema.org",
        "@type": "FAQPage",
        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "Why won't the Wi-Fi login page load?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "@type": "Answer",
              "text": "Captive portals sometimes block HTTPS handshakes or VPN/DNS profiles. Open http://nossl.sh in your browser, turn off VPNs, and retry so the network can show its sign-in splash screen."
            }
          },
          {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "What is the URL to force Wi-Fi login?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "@type": "Answer",
              "text": "Visit http://nossl.sh to trigger most captive portal login pages because it intentionally serves plain HTTP without HSTS."
            }
          },
          {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "How do I connect to the Wi-Fi login page?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "@type": "Answer",
              "text": "Turn off VPNs, then visit http://nossl.sh in a browser to trigger the captive portal. If it does not appear, reload, try a private window, or toggle Wi-Fi off/on."
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    </script>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="nossl.sh helps you diagnose no SSL connection issues, check your Wi-Fi, verify internet access, troubleshoot captive portal login pages, and inspect the headers your device sends."
    />
    <meta
      name="keywords"
      content="no ssl, nossl, never ssl alternative, captive portal login, hotel wifi login, airport wifi, coffee shop wifi, http test page"
    />
    <meta property="og:title" content="nossl.sh - Force Wi-Fi Login, Check IP & Headers (HTTP Only)" />
    <meta
      property="og:description"
      content="nossl.sh helps you diagnose no SSL connection issues, check your Wi-Fi, verify internet access, troubleshoot captive portal login pages, and inspect the headers your device sends."
    />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:url" content="http://nossl.sh/" />
    <meta property="og:site_name" content="nossl.sh" />
    <meta property="og:image" content="/static/og-image.png" />
    <meta property="og:image:alt" content="Abstract teal and navy banner for nossl.sh" />
    <meta property="og:image:width" content="1200" />
    <meta property="og:image:height" content="630" />
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
    <meta name="twitter:title" content="nossl.sh - Force Wi-Fi Login, Check IP & Headers (HTTP Only)" />
    <meta
      name="twitter:description"
      content="nossl.sh helps you diagnose no SSL connection issues, check your Wi-Fi, verify internet access, troubleshoot captive portal login pages, and inspect the headers your device sends."
    />
    <meta name="twitter:image" content="/static/og-image.png" />
    <meta name="twitter:image:alt" content="Abstract teal and navy banner for nossl.sh" />
    <title>nossl.sh - Get Wi-Fi Login & Check Your IP</title>
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" type="image/svg+xml" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/static/styles.css?v=2" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <% 
      const formattedGeneratedAt = generatedAt.toISOString().replace('T', ' ').replace(/\..+/, ' UTC');
      const headerNote = '// Trigger the captive hotel/airport Wi‑Fi login page, never HTTPS, never SSL';
      const footerLines = [
        `Prefer JSON? Try the <a href="/api/request-info" rel="nofollow">request info API endpoint</a>. Total requests served: <span class="mono">${totalRequests.toLocaleString('en-US')}</span>`
      ];
    %>
    <%- include('partials/header', {headerNote}) %>

    <main class="container page">
      <%- include('partials/connection-report') %>

      <div class="info-grid">
        <section class="card info-card" aria-labelledby="how-to-use">
          <p class="eyebrow">How to use this page</p>
          <h3 id="how-to-use" class="card__title">Plain HTTP for quick checks</h3>
          <p class="muted">See your real IP, request method, and headers without HTTPS in the way. Great for captive portals, firewall tests, or debugging VPN/proxy quirks.</p>
          <ul class="bullets">
            <li>Open http://nossl.sh to trigger captive portal pages.</li>
            <li>Share a snapshot link if support needs proof.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="muted">Need step-by-step help? Browse the <a href="/guides">full guide index</a> for hotels, cafes, and mobile walkthroughs.</p>
          <ul class="bullets">
            <li><a href="/captive-portal">Captive portal diagnostics</a></li>
            <li><a href="/wifi-login-page">Wi‑Fi login page tester</a></li>
            <li><a href="/mobile-wifi">Mobile Wi‑Fi troubleshooting</a></li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="card info-card" aria-labelledby="curl-examples">
          <p class="eyebrow">cURL examples</p>
          <h3 id="curl-examples" class="card__title">cURL IPv4/IPv6, any HTTP status</h3>
          <p class="muted">cURL your public IP - the alternative to <code class="mono">ifconfig.me</code>.</p>
          <div class="code-block">
            <code class="mono">$ curl http://nossl.sh</code>
            <button type="button" class="btn btn-outline btn-small" data-copy-text="curl http://nossl.sh">Copy</button>
            <div class="code-example mono">→ <%= clientIp %></div>
          </div>
            <p class="muted">cURL your IPv6:</p>
            <div class="code-block">
                <code class="mono">$ curl http://v6.nossl.sh</code>
                <button type="button" class="btn btn-outline btn-small" data-copy-text="curl http://v6.nossl.sh">Copy</button>
                <div class="code-example mono">→ ipv6</div>
            </div>
            <p class="muted">Check any HTTP status:</p>
          <div class="code-block">
            <code class="mono">$ curl -i http://nossl.sh/status/418</code>
            <button type="button" class="btn btn-outline btn-small" data-copy-text="curl -i http://nossl.sh/status/418">Copy</button>
            <div class="code-example mono">→ HTTP/1.1 418 I'm a Teapot</div>
          </div>
          <p class="muted">API references:</p>
          <ul class="bullets">
            <li><a href="/api/request-info" rel="nofollow">/api/request-info</a> — current IP, scheme, headers.</li>
            <li><a href="/api/counters" rel="nofollow">/api/counters</a> — request counters snapshot.</li>
            <li><a href="/api/honeypot" rel="nofollow">/api/honeypot</a> — honeypot hits as JSON.</li>
            <li><a href="/api/as/15169" rel="nofollow">/api/as/:asn</a> — ASN details, org, and prefixes.</li>
            <li><a href="/status/200" rel="nofollow">/status/:code</a> — return any HTTP status; add <code class="mono">?location=</code> for redirects.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="muted">Need the honeypot console? Visit the <a href="/honeypot">/honeypot</a> dashboard.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="card info-card" aria-labelledby="faq">
          <p class="eyebrow">FAQ</p>
          <h3 id="faq" class="card__title">Why plain HTTP?</h3>
          <dl class="faq">
            <dt>Why no TLS?</dt>
            <dd>Captive portals and restrictive networks often block HTTPS handshakes. HTTP keeps the splash page visible.</dd>
            <dt>What can I use this for?</dt>
            <dd>Spot VPN or proxy issues, capture headers for debugging, and confirm whether the network is online.</dd>
            <dt>Is there an API?</dt>
            <dd>Yes — use the <a href="/api/request-info" rel="nofollow">request info endpoint</a> for JSON.</dd>
          </dl>
        </section>
      </div>
    </main>

    <%- include('partials/footer', {formattedGeneratedAt, generationTimeMs, footerLines}) %>

    <%- include('partials/connection-report-script') %>
  </body>
</html>
